---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { WAYS } from '../site';

const stack = [
  { level: 'Production-deep', items: 'Go, Node.js, React, TypeScript, Kafka, Redis, MySQL/TiDB, Docker' },
  { level: 'Comfortable', items: 'Python, Java, PostgreSQL, Kubernetes, CI/CD, Flutter, YOLO/CUDA' },
  { level: 'AI tools', items: 'Claude, Cursor, MCP' },
];
const principles = [
  { title: 'Lead close to the work', text: 'I write code every sprint and review a lot. It keeps my decisions grounded and my reviews useful.' },
  { title: 'Grow people through real ownership', text: 'Chances to lead, to share with the wider team, and time to explore.' },
  { title: 'Connect engineering to the business', text: 'I work with product, business, and leadership on what to build, and explain trade-offs in terms of impact.' },
  { title: 'Targeted changes over rewrites', text: 'If a critical system works, I fix where it hurts instead of starting over.' },
];
---

<Base title="About" description="About John Patrick Agustin, senior engineer and tech lead.">
  <section class="page-head wrap grid">
    <h1 data-reveal>About</h1>
    <p class="lead" data-reveal>Senior engineer and tech lead. 8+ years of shipping software, five of them at Ninja Van growing from founding engineer to Engineering Manager.</p>
    <aside data-reveal>
      <p class="dot">Available now</p>
      <p>Philippines (GMT+8)</p>
      <p>BS Computer Engineering, UP Diliman</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap grid">
    <div class="prose measure body-col" data-reveal>
      <p>
        At Ninja Van I joined as one of two engineers on a new internal tools team and grew into Engineering Manager of the
        platforms team: 5–7 engineers across Singapore and India. I led the team's technical decisions, worked with
        product, business, and our CTO on what to build, and mentored three engineers into senior roles. I also started a
        company-wide frontend standards initiative that grew into its own design system team.
      </p>
      <p>
        We owned the chat and notification systems that handle hundreds of millions of events a day. I still shipped code
        every sprint, and together we <a href="/work/notification-costs">cut notification costs by over 60%</a> and{' '}
        <a href="/work/chat-notifications-rearchitecture">tripled Kafka throughput at peak</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        More recently I led a frontend team of four across Southeast Asia at an AI startup, and built an on-prem computer
        vision platform for a freelance client.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before that: 5G R&amp;D at Nokia, software in Melbourne, and leading a drone data platform in Singapore.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band wrap grid split">
    <h2 data-reveal>How I work</h2>
    <ul class="rows stacked cols content">
      {principles.map((p) => (
        <li data-reveal>
          <span class="what">{p.title}</span>
          <p class="sub">{p.text}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="pb wrap grid split">
    <h2 data-reveal>Stack</h2>
    <ul class="rows stack content">
      {stack.map((s) => (
        <li data-reveal>
          <span class="when">{s.level}</span>
          <span class="what">{s.items}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="f-sage band">
    <div class="wrap grid split">
      <h2 data-reveal>Ways to work together</h2>
      <div class="content">
        <ul class="rows stacked">
          {WAYS.map((w) => (
            <li data-reveal>
              <span class="what">{w.title}</span>
              <p class="sub">{w.text}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p data-reveal>
          Hourly or monthly contracts, part-time retainers, fixed-scope projects, or full-time contracts. I'm also open to
          the right full-time role.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
